{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>They are unclean to you</b> — and adjacent to it is <b>ואת החזיר</b>, to teach that it is forbidden to raise pigs. And <b>מבשרם לא תאכלו</b> is juxtaposed to <b>את זה תאכלו מכל אשר במים</b> — meaning: even though I forbade eating their flesh, that which is from them in the waters you may eat, for fish-blood-wine (חמרא דימא) is permitted. Another interpretation: <b>לא תאכלו — את זה תאכלו</b>, to teach that fish-entrails may be purchased only from an expert, for he reads in it <b>לא תאכלו</b> unless he says: 'this is what I purchased from So-and-so the hunter, and it is kosher.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:09:41.521003822Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}